{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/step_failures.py","reason":"new leaf module: run-scoped sink for failed LLM step calls (collect/record/drain), stdlib-only so the low runner layer can record without a layering inversion"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"record the failed call at the single seam in PydanticAIRunner.run's except block, beside the existing usage_log.record_failure, keyed by _call_label"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"activate the sink for the plan-review run scope alongside collect_contract_violations()"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"drain the sink into verdict coverage, present only when non-empty (attestation-safe)"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json","reason":"declare and describe the coverage.llm_step_failures property"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"print one text-output line for the step-failure total and per-step counts when the key is present"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_step_failures.py","reason":"new: held-out tests for record/drain round-trip, no-op outside scope, destructive drain, and the non-empty-only coverage rule"}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1786513747167700001,"uuid":"12f9b0da-83c8-419f-a365-a39cccb32382"}